**This is a textbook coverage-touching suite.** All 10 production methods are called, achieving high line coverage, but **7 of 10 tests have zero meaningful assertions**. These tests prove the code doesn't throw — nothing more. A bug in price calculation, CSV formatting, search logic, or deletion would sail through every one of them.

---

### 🔴 Critical Findings

#### 1. No Assertions (×4 tests)

These tests execute code and assert *nothing at all*:

| Test Method | Line | What It Misses |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17–21 | Never verifies the product was actually stored |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 33–36 | Never verifies the price changed to 14.99 |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39–43 | Never verifies the product is gone |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 64–66 | Never checks the count value (also tests on an empty catalog!) |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 69–74 | Never verifies discounted prices |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85–88 | Never verifies imported products exist |

**Fix — example for `AddProduct_Works`:**
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 17-21)
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_Works()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
}

// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

